! C22-6578 PROBLEM 2.6, "SORTING ON THE BASIS OF SUBFIELDS", Methods 1
! and 2 with Method 2's comment (b), printed pp.17-18 (PDF 18-19), read
! in the ink.  Method 3 is problem_2_6_method3.strap.  Method 4 is not
! run; docs/source_audit.md says why.
!
!   "Given 16 consecutive fields beginning at DATA, each of the
!   following appearance:  | A (4-bits) | B (20 bits) |
!   The four-bit subfield "A" may contain any integer number from 0
!   through 15.  Assume all A subfields are different in content, sort
!   on the basis of A subfields and put the correspondent B subfields
!   together in a string beginning at ANS."
!
! THE PRINTED STATEMENTS are Method 1 and Method 2 below as printed,
! except: no BEW, $ between blocks; Method 2's LOOP is LOOP2 and each
! block has its own ANS (ANS1..ANS4), word-aligned so a check can name
! its words; the printed ' comments are written !'.  The DATA is the
! deck's.
!
! COMMENT (b) prints three columns of first and last lines with dots
! between, "the following sets of instructions lead to the same
! results".  The left column is Method 1 itself.  The middle and right
! columns are run with the dots read as Method 1's two middle lines
! (the multiply and the store into $1) -- that reading is the deck's,
! the page prints dots.  In the left column the page prints
! "L(BU,20)(V+I), 0.20 ($)": the 2 of ($2) is missing in the ink.
!
! EXPECTED VALUES ARE HAND-DERIVED from the problem statement, not from
! the model.  Field i (i = 0..15) has
!     A = 7 2 13 0 9 15 4 11 1 14 6 3 12 8 5 10
!     B = hex B i A F i   (so B names both its position and its key)
! and the answer is the sixteen B's in order of A, 320 bits, five words:
!     B30F3 B81F8 B12F1 BB3FB B64F6 BE5FE BA6FA B07F0
!     BD8FD B49F4 BFAFF B7BF7 BCCFC B2DF2 B9EF9 B5FF5
!
! WHY (Reference Manual printed pages):
!  M1  *(BU,24): p.68, "the product ... is placed into the cleared
!      accumulator at offset 20" -- the page's 'answer at offset 20.
!      VALF is "VF, 20": an integer with no point is 20 units of the
!      field's last place, 20 BITS, which is what makes A*20 a bit
!      address.  ST(B,25,1), 17.0, 20 puts 24 bits and a sign into $1's
!      value field and sign, and ANS($1) is ANS + 20A bits.
!  M2  20A = 16A + 4A: the same 4 bits loaded at offset 22 and added at
!      offset 24.  -0.4($2) is a negative address, comment (c): "-A
!      will be assembled as 2**18-A"; the sum with $2 wraps.
!  Progressive indexing, p.21.
!
! MEASURED, against a control of 21 of 21 (five words of each of four
! answers and the halt PC): the keys of fields 0 and 1 exchanged
! (7B07F0 2B12F1 -> 2B07F0 7B12F1).  OBSERVED 8 fail, words 0 and 2 of
! each answer -- the third and eighth B's, which exchange (..B07F0 in
! word 0, ..B12F1 in word 2).  Nothing else moves.

        SLC, 1000.0
! --- Method 1 ------------------------------------------------------
ASORT   LX, $2, XW2
LOOP    L(BU, 4) (V+I), 0.04($2)
        *(BU, 24), VALF                 !'answer at offset 20
        ST(B, 25, 1), 17.0, 20          !'store into index register value field
        L(BU, 20) (V+I), 0.20($2)
        ST(BU, 20), ANS1($1)
        CB, $2, LOOP
! --- Method 2 ------------------------------------------------------
ASORT2  LX, $2, XW2A
LOOP2   L(BU, 4), -0.4($2), 20 + 2
        +(BU, 4), -0.4($2), 20 + 4
        ST(B, 25, 1), 17.0, 20
        L(BU, 20) (V+IC), 0.24($2)
        ST(BU, 20), ANS2($1)
        BZXCZ, LOOP2
! --- Method 2 comment (b), middle column ----------------------------
        LX, $2, XW2
LOOP3   L(BU, 4) (V+I), 0.24($2)
        *(BU, 24), VALF
        ST(B, 25, 1), 17.0, 20
        L(BU,20), -0.20($2)
        ST(BU,20), ANS3($1)
        CB, $2, LOOP3
! --- Method 2 comment (b), right column -----------------------------
        LX, $2, XW2A
LOOP4   L(BU, 4), -0.04($2)
        *(BU, 24), VALF
        ST(B, 25, 1), 17.0, 20
        L(BU,20) (V+IC), 0.24($2)
        ST(BU,20), ANS4($1)
        BZXCZ, LOOP4
HALT    BEW, $
XW2     XW, DATA, 16, $
VALF    VF, 20
XW2A    XW, DATA + 0.4, 16, $

        SLC, 1200.0
DATA    DD(BU,64,8), (16)7B07F02B12F1DB2D
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)F20B30F39B49F4FB
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)5FF54B64F6BB7BF7
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)1B81F8EB9EF96BA6
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)FA3BB3FBCBCCFC8B
        DD(BU,64,8), (16)D8FD5BE5FEABFAFF
        SLC, 1210.0
ANS1    DRZ(BU, 20), (16)
        SLC, 1220.0
ANS2    DRZ(BU, 20), (16)
        SLC, 1230.0
ANS3    DRZ(BU, 20), (16)
        SLC, 1240.0
ANS4    DRZ(BU, 20), (16)
        END, ASORT
